<title>INDIA: India M3 growth slows to 15.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>India M3 growth slows to 15.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Growth in India's year on year M3 money supply eased to 15.3 percent on September 27, from 16.4 percent on September 13, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.</p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Sept 27, 1996   Sept 13, 1996  Sept 29, 1995</p>
<p>		   15.3		16.4	     14.81</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,394.14 billion rupees on September 27, compared with 6,343.95 billion rupees on September 13, 1996, and 5,497.86 billion on September 29, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
